.TH DIFTRAYCTL 1
.SH NAME
diftrayctl - control a running DiftrayWM session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diftrayctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B diftrayctl
.B bar
.I "command bar text"
.br
.B diftrayctl
.B version
.br
.B diftrayctl
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diftrayctl
drives a compositor that is already running. The compositor listens on a Unix
control socket and executes one Command Bar command per connection, then
replies with the resulting status line.
.PP
Because every remote operation is a Command Bar command, the same work can be
done interactively by typing the same text after
.BR : ,
and any command registered later by a plugin or an extension stays reachable
from the shell through
.BR "diftrayctl bar" .
.PP
The socket lives at
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/diftraywm-ctl-$UID.sock
and is created mode 0700: it can restart the compositor and load code, so only
the session owner may use it.
.B DIFTRAYWM_CONTROL_SOCKET
overrides the location, which is how more than one compositor can be addressed
on the same machine.
.SH SESSION
.TP
.B exit-session
Leave the session and return to the Linux console. Aliases:
.BR session-exit ,
.BR quit .
.TP
.B restart-session
Re-execute the compositor in place, keeping the same process id, environment
and arguments. Aliases:
.BR session-restart ,
.BR restart .
.TP
.B status
Report the workspace, output, NCursors, cells, GCursors, loaded plugins and
extensions, the active configuration file, the control socket, the font and the
theme.
.SH PLUGINS AND EXTENSIONS
.TP
.BI "plugin-load " path
Load a native plugin shared library with dynalo. Its
.B diftraywm_plugin_init
runs against the same API it would get at startup, and the commands it
registers become usable immediately.
.TP
.BI "plugin-unload " path
Run a plugin's cleanup, drop the commands it registered, and unload the
library.
.TP
.B plugin-list
List loaded plugin paths.
.TP
.BI "extension-exec " path
Load and run a Lua extension. The extension may call
.BR diftray.status ,
.BR diftray.command ,
.BR diftray.on ,
and
.B diftray.register_command
at load time. Alias:
.BR extension-load .
.TP
.B extension-list
List loaded extension paths.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B config-open
Open the configuration file in use in
.BR $VISUAL ,
.BR $EDITOR ,
or
.BR vi .
The file is quoted, so paths containing spaces are safe.
.TP
.B config-path
Print the configuration file the compositor loaded.
.TP
.B config-reload
Re-read the configuration file and apply it: theme, font, help search path and
settings. The reload is atomic, so an invalid file is rejected and the running
configuration is kept.
.TP
.B config-vars
List configuration variables with their types.
.TP
.BI "config-eval " expression
Evaluate a configuration expression and print the value.
.TP
.BI "config-run " expression
Evaluate a configuration expression and execute the commands it returns.
.SH KEY REMAPPING
Every key is configured in a keymap INI file rather than in the config file, so
these act on the loaded one. See
.BR diftraywm\-keymap (5).
.TP
.B keymap-show
Print the loaded keymap, its profiles, the active profile and every binding.
Aliased as
.BR keys .
.TP
.B keymap-path
Print the path of the loaded keymap.
.TP
.B keymap-reload
Re-read the keymap file. A parse failure is reported and the previous keymap is
kept, so a broken edit cannot leave the session without keys. Aliased as
.BR reload\-keymap .
.TP
.BI keymap\-profile " name"
Switch to another profile.
.B keymap-reset
returns to the default profile.
.TP
.BI keymap\-check " path"
Parse a candidate file and report what it contains, without adopting it. This is
how to diagnose an edit before reloading it.
.TP
.BI keymap\-chord " spec"
Validate a chord spelling such as
.I <C-q>
and report the key code it resolves to, without needing a file.
.PP
System-wide remapping is not here, because it is not a Command Bar command:
it is
.BR diftrayremap (1),
a separate program that needs privileges the compositor must not have. Run
.B diftrayremap check
to see whether this machine can do it.
.SH TERMSCRIPT
.TP
.BI "source-script " path
Run a Termscript file and print the output it produced with
.BR G:puts .
Statements are terminated with semicolons, as in the bundled notelets. The
script runs on the compositor thread, so it is meant for short interactive
snippets; long-running work belongs in a notelet, which has its own worker
process. Output above 64 KiB is refused.
.SH CELLS AND MULTIPLEXER
.TP
.BI "spawn-cell " "above|below"
Create a terminal cell. Aliases:
.BR spawn-above ,
.BR spawn-below .
.TP
.B kill-cell
Remove the focused cell.
.TP
.BI "mux-split " "horizontal|vertical"
Split the focused pane below or beside it. Shortcut: Meta+S and Meta+V.
.TP
.BI "mux-focus " direction
Move multiplexer focus: next, prev, up, down, left or right. Shortcut: Meta+O
and Meta+P, and Meta+Ctrl with an arrow key.
.TP
.B mux-kill
Close the focused pane. The last pane is kept.
.TP
.B mux-zoom
Expand the focused pane to a TCursor and back. Shortcut: Meta+Z.
.TP
.B mux-list
List panes, marking the focused one with *.
.SH VIEWS, TABS AND MONITORS
.TP
.BR ncursor-list ", " ncursor-new
List NCursors and their cells, or create an NCursor.
.TP
.BR tab-next ", " tab-prev
Cycle NCursor or GCursor tabs.
.TP
.BI "workspace " number
Switch to a workspace, 1 to 10.
.TP
.B output-list
List monitors and their geometry, marking the focused one.
.TP
.BI "output-focus " "name|next|prev"
Focus a monitor.
.TP
.BI "output-move " name
Move the active NCursor and its clients to a monitor.
.TP
.BI "output-rotate " "name angle"
Rotate a monitor counter-clockwise: 0, 90, 180 or 270.
.TP
.BI "output-scale " "name scale"
Set monitor scale, 0.5 to 4.
.TP
.BI "output-position " "name x y"
Place a monitor in logical coordinates, or restore automatic placement with
.BI "output-position " "name auto"
.
.SH CURSORS AND NOTELETS
.TP
.B cursor-list
List graphical cursor identifiers, marking docked ones with *.
.TP
.BI "cursor-dock " id
Hide a graphical cursor in its Cell's Cursor Area.
.TP
.BI "cursor-restore " id
Restore a docked graphical cursor.
.TP
.BI "cursor-assign " "id F1-F4"
Bind a graphical cursor to a quick-restore key.
.TP
.BR notelet-list ", " notelet-open " " name ", " notelet-close ", " notelet-refresh
List notelets, open one in a new cell, close the active one, or re-render it.
.SH THEMING
.TP
.BI "theme-load " "file.css"
Apply a CSS theme file. See themes/default.css and themes/light.css.
.TP
.B theme-show
List the active theme properties.
.TP
.BI "set-theme " css
Apply inline CSS theme properties, for example
.RB ' ":root { border-size: 2px; }" '.
.SH HELP
.TP
.BI "help " "[page]"
Open a manual page in a cell. Without a page, the index is shown.
.SH LAUNCHER TASKBAR
The launch bar is anchored under the status bar and painted above the cells
and the graphical windows. It lists the live NCursors and GCursors of the
current workspace, marking the active one, and shows the
.B launch>
prompt while the launcher has focus. It is hidden when idle unless it is
locked.
.TP
.B lock-launchbar
Pin the launch bar to the top of the screen for the rest of the session. The
command reports "launch bar already locked" when it was already pinned.
.TP
.B unlock-launchbar
Let the launch bar hide again when the launcher is not in use.
.TP
.B toggle-launchbar
Flip between locked and unlocked.
.TP
.B launchbar-status
Report the lock state, the anchor, the bar height, whether the bar is currently
visible, and whether Caps Lock is being offered as Meta.
.PP
The equivalent Command Bar commands are
.BR "launcher lock" ,
.BR "launcher unlock" ,
.B launcher toggle
and
.BR "launcher status" .
The lock is remembered across
.B config reload
and can be preset with
.B launcher_locked
in the configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command reached the compositor and was recognised.
.TP
.B 1
The compositor did not recognise the command.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown subcommand, or a missing required argument.
.TP
.B 3
No DiftrayWM session is reachable on the control socket.
.PP
Handlers report their own failures in the printed status line, for example
"plugin load failed: ...". Scripts should read the text as well as the status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFTRAYWM_CONTROL_SOCKET
Control socket path, overriding the default under XDG_RUNTIME_DIR.
.SH SEE ALSO
diftraywm(1),
.BR diftray.conf (5),
GUIDE.md,
CONFIGURATION.md
